To build the sources you need to set the following environment variables:

BUILD_DRIVE to whichever drive holds the source tree e.g. SET BUILD_DRIVE=E:
BUILD_ROOT full path to this directory e.g. SET BUILD_ROOT=E:\3DFXCDGC\GLIDE\SRC
MASM To the install directory for Microsoft Assember VERSION 6.11 ( or greater )
           eg. SET MASM=C:\DEVEL\MASM611
DIRECTXSDK to the DirectX SDK directory eg. SET DIRECTXSDK=C:\DEVEL\DXSDK\SDK

If you are using Microsot C set MSVC to the install directory for Microsoft 
eg. SET MSVC=C:\devel\msdev

If you are using Watcom set the environment variable WATCOM to the install directory 
for Watcom C/C++ 10.6 or greater e.g. SET WATCOM=C:\devel\WATCOM

Then run the setup.bat file with an argument of:

MSVC for Microsoft C
WATWIN for Watcom Windows build
WATDOS for Watcom DOS build

You should build the directories in the following order:

GCI
SWLIBS\TEXUS
SWLIBS\ARCADE

You can then build any of the demos. The demos are designed to run under Windows 95 only.

To run the demos you need to copy them to the corrsponding directory under atb_demos
